---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { site } from "../data/config";

/**
 * Ported from the droparabia-landing terms.
 *
 * The one clause NOT copied is droparabia's 90-day refund guarantee. It is a
 * specific promise about a different, paid product, and this page sells
 * nothing — the webinar is free. Section 2 says so instead. When the paid
 * cohort has its own checkout, its refund terms belong with that purchase, and
 * the droparabia wording is the right starting point for them.
 */
---

<LegalPage
	title={`Terms and conditions — ${site.name}`}
	description={`The terms that apply when you register for the free ${site.name} webinar.`}
	heading="Terms and conditions"
	updated="October 2026"
>
	<p>By registering for our webinar or using this site, you agree to the following terms.</p>

	<section>
		<h2>1. Registration and access</h2>
		<p>
			When you register, we send you a link to attend the webinar. That link is for your
			personal use and is not transferable. Sharing it, or recording, republishing or
			redistributing the webinar in any form, is not permitted.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>2. The webinar is free</h2>
		<p>
			There is no charge to attend and nothing to pay on this site. If we later offer a paid
			program, its own terms — including anything about payment and refunds — will be shown
			to you before you buy, and you will have to accept them separately.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>3. No guarantee of results</h2>
		<p>
			Our material is educational. Figures we mention describe past work by our team and
			students; they are not a promise of what you will earn or achieve. What you get out of
			it depends on your own effort, skill and circumstances.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>4. Attendance</h2>
		<p>
			The webinar runs live at the advertised time. Replays are not guaranteed, so register
			only if you intend to attend. We may change the date or time, and if we do we will tell
			everyone who has registered.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
		<p>
			Everything presented in the webinar and published on this site — including the
			training material, student project videos, text and brand marks — is protected by
			copyright. You may not reproduce, republish, resell or distribute any part of it.
			Student projects shown remain the property of the students who made them.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>6. Removing access</h2>
		<p>
			We may cancel a registration or remove someone from the webinar if these terms are
			broken, including abusive behaviour, disruption, or sharing access with others.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Any questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</LegalPage>
